# scr5-dispOff-hmmm-rdCpu222-2e  CPU VRAM request cycles
# Comments carry no information; everything the arbiter needs is on a
# keyword line. 'requests' comes last and is followed by that many
# body lines, one per request: the VDP cycle on which the arbiter
# latched it, in RAS numbering with the same origin as the .txt grid
# (cas = line*col + row), and for an interleaved rdwrCpu capture an
# r or w suffix saying whether it was a read or a write.
# Requests that cause no visible access are included and must be kept:
# the arbiter drops some, and some are granted outside the .txt
# window. Which ones is derived by the model, not recorded here.
# 'margin' is the whole drop rule: a request is taken only if it
# arrives at least that many cycles after the slot the request
# before it was granted. It is negative with sprites on.
capture scr5-dispOff-hmmm-rdCpu222-2e
mode dispOff
line 1368
need 16
need_row 170 16
margin 2
buffer 1
policy drop-new
kind r
requests 38
